  "scope": "Canada — Ontario first. Anishinaabemowin (Ojibwe) entries sourced from the Ojibwe People's Dictionary. Designed for extension to Kanien'kéha (Mohawk), Cree (nēhiyawēwin / ililīmowin), and other Indigenous languages of Turtle Island.",
  "acknowledgment": "Indigenous names for birds are gifts from First Nations, Métis, and Inuit communities. They belong to those communities — we host citations and pronunciations here with reverence and attribution, and link back to the community-led sources that hold them.",
  "principles": [
    "Every name is cited to a community-led or community-sanctioned source.",
    "Dialect and spelling vary by community — we name the source community wherever known.",
    "If we don't have a verified name for a species in a language, we say so plainly. We do not fabricate.",
    "Audio pronunciations link back to the source dictionary so the speaker's labour and consent stays visible."
  ],
